```js
// Initialize the React state manager with your app’s configuration
const { store, context, hooks } = manageReactState(
  {
    initialState: initialStateObject,
    reducers: reducersMap,
    middlewares: [loggerMiddleware],
    enhancers: [applyMiddleware('myMiddleWare')]
  },
  store,                     // the store instance that will be created
  context,                   // the React context that will be created
  { useStateSelectorHook, useDispatchActionHook }   // custom hooks for components
);
```

This single line creates the store, the React context, and exposes the custom hooks (`useStateSelectorHook` and `useDispatchActionHook`) for use throughout your component tree.

